---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Open Claw Integration — inbox.dog" description="Give your Open Claw agent Gmail access with inbox.dog.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <p class="text-sm text-primary-400 mb-2"><a href="/docs" class="hover:text-primary-600">&larr; Docs</a></p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-primary-900">inbox.dog for Open Claw</h1>
    <p class="text-primary-600 mb-8"><strong>Give your <a href="https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw" class="text-primary-900 underline">Open Claw</a> agent production-ready Gmail access in 60 seconds.</strong> Read, search, and send emails via MCP. OAuth-native (no passwords), CASA Tier 2 certified, zero custom code.</p>

    <section class="mb-10 p-6 bg-primary-50 border border-primary-200 rounded-xl">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3">TL;DR — What you get</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-primary-600 text-sm space-y-1">
        <li><strong>5 Gmail tools:</strong> <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">read_emails</code>, <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">read_email</code>, <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">search_emails</code>, <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">send_email</code>, <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">get_profile</code></li>
        <li><strong>Setup time:</strong> Add one MCP endpoint (<code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">https://inbox.dog/mcp</code>), restart gateway, test with one prompt</li>
        <li><strong>Auth:</strong> OAuth via MCP (no password storage), CASA Tier 2 certified for security compliance</li>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> $0.10 per OAuth flow, 10 free credits, self-host option available</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-primary-900">60-second setup (recommended)</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">1) Add inbox.dog MCP server</h3>
      <p class="text-primary-600 mb-3">Edit <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">~/.openclaw/openclaw.json</code>:</p>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code class="language-json">{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "inbox-dog": {
      "url": "https://inbox.dog/mcp"
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">2) Restart Open Claw gateway</h3>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code class="language-bash">{`openclaw gateway restart`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">3) Trigger auth + verify</h3>
      <p class="text-primary-600 mb-3">Ask your agent:</p>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code>{`What's my email address?`}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="text-primary-600">Open Claw will start OAuth in your browser on first use. After consent, tools are ready.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 p-6 bg-primary-50 border border-primary-200 rounded-xl">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3">Agent prompt (copy/paste)</h2>
      <p class="text-primary-600 text-sm mb-3">Add this to your agent's system prompt or knowledge base for optimal tool usage:</p>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code>{`You have Gmail access via inbox.dog MCP (https://inbox.dog/mcp).

Available tools: get_profile, read_emails, search_emails, read_email, send_email.

Usage pattern:
1. Use get_profile to confirm email address
2. Use search_emails for specific queries, read_emails for recent messages
3. Use read_email to get full message content (requires message ID)
4. ALWAYS ask confirmation before send_email unless user says "send now"

These tools use OAuth - the human will authenticate once on first use.`}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-primary-900">Why agents trust inbox.dog</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-primary-600 space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><strong>OAuth-first architecture:</strong> MCP Authorization spec with PKCE + dynamic client registration (no password storage or transmission)</li>
        <li><strong>Security certified:</strong> CASA Tier 2 certified for Gmail restricted scopes (annual security assessment required)</li>
        <li><strong>Production-ready:</strong> HTTPS + HSTS, structured error handling, rate limiting built-in</li>
        <li><strong>Flexible deployment:</strong> Use hosted service or self-host for full control</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-primary-600 text-sm mt-3">More: <a href="/blog/casa-tier-2-gmail-oauth" class="text-primary-900 underline">CASA certification details</a> · <a href="https://github.com/acoyfellow/inbox.dog" class="text-primary-900 underline">Self-host on GitHub</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-primary-900">Alternative: Workspace Skill (optional)</h2>
      <p class="text-primary-600 mb-4"><strong>Note:</strong> The MCP setup above is recommended for most users. Use this alternative only if you need explicit workspace skill configuration or custom environment variables.</p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">1) Create skill folder</h3>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code class="language-bash">{`mkdir -p ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/inbox-dog`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">2) Create an API key</h3>
      <p class="text-primary-600 mb-3">Generate your <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">INBOXDOG_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">INBOXDOG_CLIENT_SECRET</code>:</p>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code class="language-bash">{`curl -s -X POST https://inbox.dog/api/keys \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"name": "openclaw"}' | jq`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-3 mt-6">3) Configure credentials</h3>
      <p class="text-primary-600 mb-3">Add to <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">~/.openclaw/openclaw.json</code>:</p>
      <div class="bg-primary-900 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <pre class="text-primary-100 font-mono"><code class="language-json">{`{
  "skills": {
    "entries": {
      "inbox-dog": {
        "enabled": true,
        "env": {
          "INBOXDOG_CLIENT_ID": "id_your_client_id_here",
          "INBOXDOG_CLIENT_SECRET": "sk_your_client_secret_here"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-primary-900">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-primary-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-1">No email tools appear</h3>
          <p class="text-primary-600 text-sm">Restart gateway and recheck the MCP block in <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">openclaw.json</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-primary-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-1">OAuth fails</h3>
          <p class="text-primary-600 text-sm">Validate your key: <code class="bg-primary-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">curl -s https://inbox.dog/api/keys/YOUR_CLIENT_ID -H "X-Client-Secret: YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET"</code>. Then retry auth.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-primary-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-primary-900 mb-1">Need deeper docs</h3>
          <p class="text-primary-600 text-sm"><a href="/docs/guides/mcp" class="text-primary-900 underline">MCP guide</a> · <a href="/docs/api" class="text-primary-900 underline">API reference</a> · <a href="/docs/errors" class="text-primary-900 underline">Error codes</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
